   "evidence": "Polynomial.lean:147-154 `mulVec_signCount` is stated with `Matrix.of fun i c => \u220f j, (columns c j : \u2124) ^ rows i j` and integer `signCount`/`signSum`; Polynomial.lean:139 `private theorem signSum_prod_pow`; Moments.lean:49 `eq_fiberCount` and :62 `pos_iff_exists` have no polynomial counterpart (grep `eq_signCount|signCount_pos_of` in code/TauCeti: no hits). Roadmap README.md:313-315 requires 'restrict to realized sign columns ... prove rank and invertibility of the adapted square matrix' with inverse over \u211a (README.md:311-312).",
   "file": "TauCeti/Geometry/RealAlgebraic/SignDetermination/Polynomial.lean",
   "fix": "Generalize `mulVec_signCount` to a coefficient ring `K` with `[Ring K]` (cast `signSum` into `K`, as `fullInverse_mulVec_signSum` already does for \u211a), and add the polynomial-level `eq_signCount` and positivity corollary mirroring `eq_fiberCount`/`pos_iff_exists`. Alternatively make `signSum_prod_pow` public so consumers can instantiate the generic lemmas directly.",
   "issue": "Moments.lean exports three generic results (mulVec_fiberCount, eq_fiberCount, pos_iff_exists) but Polynomial.lean specializes only the first, and only over \u2124 (`mulVec_signCount`). The roadmap's restricted-column step inverts with a rational matrix, so a consumer must re-derive the \u211a moment identity and the uniqueness/positivity corollaries at polynomial data; the only bridge (`signSum_prod_pow`, line 139) is `private`, so `eq_fiberCount`/`pos_iff_exists` cannot be instantiated with `signSum`/`tarskiQuery` moments without reproving it.",
